            "normalized_html": "<p>First, notice that all of the terms have a common factor of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x.]</span> To simplify the computation, we can factor out the <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x,]</span> as follows:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: x^3 - 6x^2 + 9x = x(x^2 - 6x + 9)]</span></p><p>The expression <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x^2 - 6x + 9]</span> is a perfect square trinomial that can be factored as follows:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: x(x^{2} \u2212 6x + 9)|=; x(x^{2} \u2212 6x + 3^{2})|=; x(x^{2} \u2212 2 \u22c5 3x + 3^{2})|=; x(x \u2212 3)^{2}]</span></p>",
