          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Note that all of the terms have a common factor of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x.]</span> To simplify the computation, we can factor out the <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x,]</span> as follows:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: x^{3} + x^{2} \u2212 2x|= x(x^{2} + x \u2212 2)]</span></p><p>Now, we factor the polynomial <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x^2 + x - 2]</span> as follows:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: x(x^{2} + x \u2212 2)|=; x((x^{2} \u2212 x) + (2x \u2212 2))|=; x(x(x \u2212 1) + 2(x \u2212 1))|=; x(x + 2)(x \u2212 1)]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Note that all of the terms have a common factor of [MATH: x.] To simplify the computation, we can factor out the [MATH: x,] as follows:\n\n[MATH: x^{3} + x^{2} \u2212 2x|= x(x^{2} + x \u2212 2)]\n\nNow, we factor the polynomial [MATH: x^2 + x - 2] as follows:\n[MATH: x(x^{2} + x \u2212 2)|=; x((x^{2} \u2212 x) + (2x \u2212 2))|=; x(x(x \u2212 1) + 2(x \u2212 1))|=; x(x + 2)(x \u2212 1)]",
